Debian 13 independent module qualification: 2026-10-01
====================================================

Copyright 2026 Qore Technologies, s.r.o.

Result: PASS for development snapshots from 31 of the 36 independent module
repositories on native amd64 and arm64 (aarch64 Linux on hoppy). This comprises
UUID from QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13, the original 24-module batch below, and the
six-module dependency chain described in the additional qualification section.
These are unsigned local packages, not final releases or a published archive.

Qore SDK/runtime: 3.0.0~git20261001.1-0qore1~deb13.
Evidence bundle: qore-debian13-modules-20261001 under the qualification hosts'
temporary directory. QUALIFICATION.json records exact package versions, source
commits, packaging-overlay hashes and per-architecture reports. QUALIFICATION.txt
summarizes the results. Each module has debian/QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13, and audits/
records all 71 audit-changes checks. commits.json records module push verification.

Qualified modules
-----------------

amqp, cairo, fsevent, geos, git, imagemagick, kalman, magic, msgpack, mysql,
ncurses, odbc, openldap, pgsql, sqlite3, ssh, ssh2, sybase (freetds), sysconf,
tar, treesitter, vss, zip and zmq. UUID was qualified with the core SDK earlier.
The additional chain qualifies process, xml, python, xmlsec, proj and nats.
Bundled modules, including JSON and YAML, remain part of Qore's packages.

Original 24-module batch checks
------------------------------

- All 24 source packages reproduce from independent preparations.
- Each module passes two full offline, unprivileged builds on each CPU,
  using different paths and parallelism and varied incoming locale/timezone.
  All 146 first-build binary artifacts reproduce byte-for-byte on their CPU.
- Each module also passes a clean architecture-only (-B) build without
  Doxygen or Graphviz. Its packages match the full builds exactly.
  Totals: 96 full builds and 48 architecture-only builds.
- All 25 architecture-independent packages match across amd64 and arm64.
- Source/binary Lintian has no errors. Binary checking uses the pinned
  Lintian 2.129 checker with the Debian profile in a separate offline image.
  Artifact manifests, ELF hardening, detached debug symbols and Qore AOT
  metadata pass inspection on both CPUs.
- All 96 installed autopkgtest executions pass offline as an unprivileged
  user. Minimal runtime installation without libqore-dev, exact coinstallation
  of documentation/debug packages, dpkg verification, purge, autoremove and
  SDK-free reinstall pass individually for every module on both CPUs.
- Combined installation of 76 artifacts from all 25 repositories passes
  on both CPUs. All 55 native/AOT module names load together in forward and
  reverse order in fresh tiered and AST processes, using only installed /usr
  modules, without the SDK or network access. Installed file verification passes.

Corrections found by qualification
----------------------------------

The ncurses and tar packages produced different AOT objects when build
parallelism changed. Their recipes now fix QCC_JOBS=1 and remove an inherited
QCC_SPLIT_THRESHOLD; independent make targets still build in parallel. Fsevent
receives the same missing reproducibility policy. OpenLDAP's unprivileged
fixture now invokes /usr/sbin/slapd because /usr/sbin is absent from that user's
default PATH. All four corrected source candidates pass the checks above.
Their source manifests preserve the frozen, precommit packaging overlays.

Two issues were in the qualification driver: ImageMagick's own common package
must be available to APT, and SSH/SSH2 tests can consume a driver's piped stdin.
The corrected driver uses a local package index and passes scripts as command
arguments with closed stdin. Original failures and corrected runs are retained.

Additional six-module qualification
-----------------------------------

Evidence bundles: qore-debian13-module-chain-20261001 and
qore-debian13-module-deps-20261001, with the same Qore SDK/runtime as above.
The chain's QUALIFICATION.json records exact module commits, source versions,
packaging overlays, dependency reports, combined installation and audit records.
PROJ includes upstream documentation/CMake fixes from commit 2a36e61eca54.

- All six source packages reproduce independently. 24 full offline builds
  and 12 architecture-only builds pass across both CPUs. All
  36 first-build artifacts reproduce on their CPU; all 6 architecture-
  independent packages also match across CPUs. Architecture-only builds omit
  Doxygen/Graphviz and reproduce the full-build binaries.
- All 26 installed autopkgtest executions pass, including PROJ/Python
  coexistence. Minimal SDK-free installation, exact debug/documentation package
  coinstallation, file verification, purge, autoremove and reinstall pass.
- Source/binary Lintian, ELF hardening, detached debug information and AOT
  metadata checks pass. Each module's qualification file records its scope.
- Combined installation now covers 94 artifacts from all 31 repositories.
  All 82 native/AOT names load together in both orders in fresh tiered and
  AST processes, offline and without the SDK. Installed file verification passes.

Boost 1.90 (1.90.0-6.1~qore4~deb13.1) and NATS C
(3.13.0-2~qore2~deb13.1) add 111 dependency artifacts per CPU. Both backports
pass two full native offline builds, source/binary Lintian, exact binary
reproducibility, hardening/debug inspection and installed tests before and
after purge/autoremove/reinstall. Boost runs all 26 Debian installed-library
tests; NATS exercises pub/sub, request/reply and JetStream revision history.

Existing Debian Boost 1.83 and NATS 3.10 clients remain usable after installing
the newer SDKs, with their original runtimes and loader paths preserved.
Boost 1.83/1.90 filesystem libraries also pass same-process operations in
both load orders. These checks do not establish compatibility for every
possible Boost consumer; the exact tested scope is retained with the evidence.

Qualification caught premature stripping and missing linker hardening in the
Boost.Build bootstrap. The recipe now passes Debian flags to its supported
cxx toolset and lets debhelper split debug symbols. Bootstrap failures propagate;
the redundant unversioned g++ dependency is removed. The CMake generator
uses relative installed paths, and assembly receives debug-prefix mapping,
so the SDK and Boost.Context reproduce across build directories. NATS C uses
an explicit /usr/sbin/nats-server path; the Qore NATS fixtures declare the system PATH for
unprivileged users. The qualification driver also needed XML's separate
libxml2 orig component, prepared by its existing pinned-source repacker. This
required no XML code change. Original failures and corrected candidates are
retained.

Remaining work
--------------

Five repositories still need Debian qualification: grpc, pdf, v8, jni and
oracle. Remaining dependency work includes PyArrow, PDFium and the Node/V8
stack. Boost 1.90, NATS C and the process/XML/Python/XMLSec/PROJ chain pass the
additional qualification above.
JNI retains the approved pinned-JAR policy. Oracle dependency hosting and
the optional V8 app catalogue's redistribution review remain separate gates.

No prior Debian upgrade/ABI baseline is available. Only the service scenarios
exercised by package tests are qualified. Final ABI/release freeze, acceptance
of exact release artifacts, dependency maintenance and durable evidence
retention remain required. Public Debian delivery needs a signed Debian archive;
an Ubuntu PPA does not publish these packages.
